    "28": {
      "date": "2026-11-08",
      "edition": "Sunday 8 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Opponent watch",
          "heading": "Farrell says Ireland are 'raising the standard' before meeting Fiji",
          "body": "Ireland head coach Farrell called Friday's 30-point win over Argentina a 'good night at the office' and said the squad is clearer on the standard it wants. \"I suppose it's raising the standard to be as good as we possibly can.\" The win moved Ireland top of the northern hemisphere table for at least 24 hours. It followed a 40-21 defeat by the All Blacks at Eden Park, Ireland's previous outing. Fiji are next on the schedule."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
          "heading": "New Zealand beat Scotland 43-21 to extend winning run",
          "body": "Wales edge Japan 28-21 in autumn opener. England's George Furbank returns for Australia after injury absence."
        }
      ],
      "source": {
        "name": "RTÉ Sport Rugby"
      }
    },
    "386": {
      "date": "2026-11-08",
      "edition": "Sunday 8 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Selection call",
          "heading": "George Furbank returns to England's side for Australia after injury-hit absence",
          "body": "England's 23-man squad for Sunday's Nations Championship match with Australia has been confirmed, and Furbank's return is the headline change: the full-back has been out of the Test side since November 2024 through injuries and a bout of appendicitis in the July window. Fin Smith has been deemed fit to play after a scare in the build-up, having started each of England's past five outings at fly-half. Greg Fisilau, the Exeter Chiefs back-rower, is in the matchday squad and, according to Planet Rugby's selection review, in line to win a maiden cap."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
          "heading": "New Zealand beat Scotland 43-21 to extend winning run",
          "body": "Wales edge Japan 28-21 in autumn opener."
        }
      ],
      "source": {
        "name": "Planet Rugby"
      }
    },
    "387": {
      "date": "2026-11-08",
      "edition": "Sunday 8 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Team news",
          "heading": "Antoine Dupont captains injury-hit France, Kalvin Gourgues wins first start against Fiji",
          "body": "Fabien Galthié named Antoine Dupont as captain at scrum-half for Saturday's match against Fiji in Lyon, with Romain Ntamack at flyhalf, their first start together at half-back since March 2025. Dupont wrestled the number nine jersey from Maxime Lucu, who drops to the bench. Kalvin Gourgues, who has come off the bench four times, makes his first start in midfield alongside Yoram Moefana. Emmanuel Meafou, Thibaud Flament, Matthieu Jalibert and Fabien Brau-Boirie were all sidelined for the November internationals."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
          "heading": "New Zealand beat Scotland 43-21 to extend winning run",
          "body": "Wales edge Japan 28-21 in autumn opener. England's George Furbank returns for Australia after injury absence."
        }
      ],
      "match": {
        "venue": "Groupama Stadium, Lyon"
      },
      "source": {
        "name": "Planet Rugby"
      }
    },
    "388": {
      "date": "2026-11-08",
      "edition": "Sunday 8 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Coaching verdict",
          "heading": "Andy Farrell admits Ireland missed chance to be ruthless against Argentina",
          "body": "Ireland had 59 per cent of the territory against Argentina yet did not score after the 55th minute, when Ronan Kelleher finished a rolling maul. Farrell's post-match verdict was blunt: \"I think the story of the game is we missed a chance to be ruthless.\" He admitted the side must improve if they are to challenge at next year's World Cup in Australia, with Fiji up next and then the world champion Springboks."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
          "heading": "New Zealand beat Scotland 43-21 to extend winning run",
          "body": "Wales edge Japan 28-21 in autumn opener. England's George Furbank returns for Australia after injury absence."
        }
      ],
      "source": {
        "name": "BBC Rugby Union"
      }
    },
    "389": {
      "date": "2026-11-08",
      "edition": "Sunday 8 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Post-match review",
          "heading": "Quesada calls Springboks' first half among best in recent times",
          "body": "Italy's head coach said Saturday's Turin defeat came against the best team in the world, and that South Africa's first half was among the best played in recent times. He credited his forwards' finishing of phases and defence on the driving maul. The kicking game and clearance kicks did not work, and in some situations Italy put themselves under pressure. The team got partly back into the match until the 70th minute, with more possession and a good try, and Quesada said the lessons matter before three important fixtures."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
          "heading": "New Zealand beat Scotland 43-21 to extend winning run",
          "body": "Wales edge Japan 28-21 in autumn opener. England's George Furbank returns for Australia after injury absence."
        }
      ],
      "source": {
        "name": "Federazione Italiana Rugby"
      }
    },
    "390": {
      "date": "2026-11-08",
      "edition": "Sunday 8 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Captain's admission",
          "heading": "Sione Tuipulotu takes full responsibility for Scotland's discipline after All Blacks defeat",
          "body": "Captain Sione Tuipulotu has spoken of his own role in the second-half fade. Sin-binned on 50 minutes, he said: \"Our discipline wasn't good enough, and it starts with me. I got sent to the bin and 10 minutes with your captain off isn't good for any team. I take full responsibility for that.\" Scotland conceded 13 penalties to New Zealand's eight and scored nothing after the interval in the 43-21 Murrayfield defeat, with Tuipulotu admitting they were \"nowhere near accurate enough\" in that period."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
          "heading": "Wales edge Japan 28-21 in autumn opener",
          "body": "England's George Furbank returns for Australia after injury absence."
        }
      ],
      "source": {
        "name": "BBC Rugby Union"
      }
    },
    "391": {
      "date": "2026-11-08",
      "edition": "Sunday 8 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Autumn result",
          "heading": "Josh Adams scores twice as Wales edge Japan 28-21 in Cardiff",
          "body": "Wales survived a nervy finish to open their autumn campaign, with Steve Tandy's side made to sweat by Japan late on. Archie Griffin, the tighthead prop, opened the scoring after four minutes, and Louis Rees-Zammit ended an eight-Test tryless run with his first Welsh try of 2026 just before the break. Blair Murray's break from a loose Japan kick set up Tomos Williams for Josh Adams's second try, but a late Japan try brought the margin back to one score. Wales held on for a bonus-point victory."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
          "heading": "New Zealand beat Scotland 43-21 to extend winning run",
          "body": "England's George Furbank returns for Australia after injury absence."
        }
      ],
      "source": {
        "name": "WalesOnline"
      }
    },
    "460": {
      "date": "2026-11-08",
      "edition": "Sunday 8 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Discipline problems",
          "heading": "Efraín Elías and Justo Piccardo yellow-carded as Pumas forward pack thins out",
          "body": "Justo Piccardo was yellow-carded for offside on 34 minutes, leaving Argentina down to 14 men. Efraín Elías was later yellow-carded for a high tackle on Hugo Keenan, and Ireland's final try came against a seven-man Pumas pack. Leonel Oviedo also went off for a head injury assessment in the first half, returning after about four minutes. The 42-12 defeat was Argentina's third in four."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
          "heading": "New Zealand beat Scotland 43-21 to extend winning run",
          "body": "Wales edge Japan 28-21 in autumn opener. England's George Furbank returns for Australia after injury absence."
        }
      ],
      "source": {
        "name": "Americas Rugby News"
      }
    },
    "461": {
      "date": "2026-11-08",
      "edition": "Sunday 8 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Captain's call",
          "heading": "Harry Wilson urges Wallabies to 'play our own game' against England",
          "body": "Ahead of Sunday's opener at Twickenham, the captain said the Wallabies must be themselves: \"We definitely want to be us.\" Wilson pointed to the 42-38 win over South Africa in Perth, when Australia scored five tries and backed their skills, even after being reduced to 11 men. He said the two New Zealand defeats, where the Wallabies conceded 93 points, had taught valuable lessons. Coach Les Kiss warned that England's back three \"can do damage\" if given space."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
          "heading": "New Zealand beat Scotland 43-21 to extend winning run",
          "body": "Wales edge Japan 28-21 in autumn opener."
        }
      ],
      "match": {
        "venue": "Allianz Stadium, Twickenham, London",
        "referee": "Pierre Brousset"
      }
    },
    "463": {
      "date": "2026-11-08",
      "edition": "Sunday 8 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Selection call",
          "heading": "Riku Kitahara started at fly-half for Japan in their defeat to Wales",
          "body": "Japan went into Saturday's match in Cardiff without three of their first-choice fly-halves: Sam Greene and Seung-sin Lee were injured, and Ryunosuke Ito, who had started all of Japan's Tests in 2026, was back at university and missed the tour. Japan coach Eddie Jones gave the No. 10 jersey to uncapped Honda Heat fly-half Riku Kitahara, with Toyota's Shinya Komura, the only other fly-half on tour, on the bench. Komura's try four minutes from time made it a one-score game, but Wales held on for a 28-21 win."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
          "heading": "New Zealand beat Scotland 43-21 to extend winning run",
          "body": "England's George Furbank returns for Australia after injury absence."
        }
      ],
